{
  "format_version": 1,
  "kind": "csv-import",
  "description": "Hand-derived vectors for CSV import (docs/spec/05, section 'CSV details'). The Python importer (backend/recruit_radar/services/csv_io.py) and the TypeScript importer (src/engine/csv.ts) must both reproduce every case. Row cells are [explicit observed_at or null, company_name, title, location, work_mode, department, url, posted_at, source_posting_id]; rows are listed by effective observed_at ascending (a blank observed_at counts as the import time), then file order. errors are unique [line, field-or-null] pairs sorted by line then field; warnings are [line, kind] pairs. A text given as an object is expanded by the harness: {repeat:{head,row,count}} = head + row.replace('{i}', i) for i in 0..count-1; {pad:{head,fill,total_bytes,bom}} = optional BOM + head + fill repeated (then 'x' to reach the byte length exactly); {parts:[...]} = the concatenation of literal strings and {fill,count} runs. expected.rows null means the rows are not compared. Python and the TypeScript importer take the same imported_at.",
  "imported_at": "2026-10-13T12:00:00Z",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "csv-01-plain",
      "description": "Two required columns, one row. Optional fields are null, work_mode defaults to unknown.",
      "text": "company_name,title\nAcme,Engineer\n",
      "expected": {
        "file_error": null,
        "accepted": 1,
        "rejected": 0,
        "rows": [[null, "Acme", "Engineer", null, "unknown", null, null, null, null]],
        "errors": [],
        "warnings": []
      }
    },
